y in the stealth section  here and so it actually appears on the  square button and it only appears here  in this contextual situation so when  you're sneaking around you sneak up  behind this guy and then you can pers  Square for petrificus totalis one of the  game's Biggest Mysteries continues to be  the ancient magic and our character's  connection to it you can even use the  mysterious powerful magic your  professors do not understand to  obliterate your strongest foes as you  chain combo attacks against enemies and  collect the blue magical Aura Left  Behind after some fights you'll power up  your ancient magic meter once it reaches  the halfway point you'll be able to  trigger an incredibly powerful attack  using L1 and R1 in the Showcase we see  this manifest itself in three different  attacks one that has this sort of  exploding effect and then another one  that's just completely makes the enemy  disappears this sort of black smokey  effect and then one that turns the enemy  into a chicken now as we have seen a few  things already changed since that very  first reveal trailer I do feel like I  need to point out this spell here which  is most likely glacias there's a  possibility maybe impedimenta as well I  still think glacias is the most likely  candidate however I will caution folks  to say that it is very possible things  could have changed clearly this spell  was at one point in the game maybe it's  still in the game and it's one of these  unknown slots that we don't know about  yet but seeing that there have already  been a few changes we've noticed from  that initial trailer also important to  keep in mind that anything could change  and if you want to see the absolute best  look we've gotten yet at uninterrupted  combat the second gameplay showcase  where they walk through that dark arts  battle arena is by far the best place to  see it in that very same showcase they  also gave an incredible breakdown of the  open world and I have a video breaking  a